# ra02 AND ra03 ARE SWAP NOW, SO THEIR 0100 IS CLEAR -- minor 2 and 3, not
# 66 and 67.  The bit marks a bitmapped FILESYSTEM and is set per partition:
# ra01, every machine's partition b, is minor 1 for exactly this reason.
# ipnx-v10.m declares `swap ra 02' and `swap ra 03' (alice.m:5-6's two 122 MB
# areas), and sw.c:107-113 compares the node's i_rdev against swdevt[].sw_dev
